{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/gondola/pulls/14","id":5095364243,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVcgH888AAAABL7UWkw","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/pull/14","diff_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/pull/14.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/pull/14.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/gondola/issues/14","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/gondola/pulls/14/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/gondola/pulls/14/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/gondola/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/gondola/issues/14/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/gondola/statuses/49cc2b96c8817a47319d5b7bd484184a22fa984b","number":14,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Compile Go-owned subtree lifecycle and cancellation across React and DOM","user":{"login":"samuelpmahan","id":32501459,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTAxNDU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32501459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This extends PR #13's actual compiled Go path to a finite Parent → Child → Grandchild lifecycle plus an independent Sibling. Go owns request generations, identity, counters, subtree removal/remount and ordered cancellation. React and standalone DOM render the same compiled application contract.\n\nThe shared host now supports an explicit closed effect policy, correlation retirement and typed GoScript effect-slice normalization through the existing generated encoder and Update result TypeID. Ordinary Go `append` remains in application code. Default effect validation stays strict. A reentrant-unmount wrapper bug and a clean-checkout test dependency were repaired with independent reviews.\n\nStacked on `codex/gobi-compiled-methods-20261031` at `6b49cc0bd4c9512a041f723c86b632ec506afd9d`. Published source `49cc2b96c8817a47319d5b7bd484184a22fa984b`, tree `d49ca35b7eda23837c392bbe0d2363551e4c7bec`; local alias `1d94f3f287a13eea8c67dda85cf73e94439a6da2` has the exact same tree and direct parent.\n\n### Executed so far\n\n- Fresh **explicit partial** `bash run-compiled-lifecycle.sh --lifecycle-only`: 18 commands, 13 stages, 122 stable source pins, zero failures; both real CLI builds produced 67 files with identical AppIR/encoder and separately pinned raw bundles.\n- Native Go, direct emitted module, mounted React, DOM and alternating profiles matched: 26 ticks, 16 clicks, 17 swaps, seven requests, three Grandchild→Child→Parent cancellations, 18 retained detached-button probes, and eight detected mutation controls. Sixteen swaps had callback witnesses (32 fences); one fixed swap checks root/state/pending preservation without a fabricated callback.\n- Final HTTP demo passed; actual Go state, tree, requests/cancellation, sibling survival, remounts, duplicate replies, disabled controls and backend switches are inspectable. No browser errors or WASM.\n- Root independently ran 47 targeted Node tests and both native Go test packages successfully. Typed-effect, unmount, oracle metadata and explicit fresh-appDir repairs have separate preserved findings and acceptance receipts.\n- Milestone0 checksum manifest and all23 tracked source entries are byte-identical to milestone commit ed3; the generated24th entry and 5,000-case replay require terminal regression evidence.\n\n### Pending full acceptance\n\nThis remains a **draft**. The default full CI command is newly launched. A local full parent was explicitly invalidated after a workflow indentation error and an ignored-preflight dependency in the compiled-module tests were discovered; its inherited child continues independently. That parent is not a pass. The corrected runner builds fresh outputs before running those tests through `GOBI_LIFECYCLE_APP_DIR`. The completed lifecycle-only command is not substituted for the inherited suite.\n\nComplete raw failed/accepted traces, screenshots, manifests, versions, exact commands and final cross-review acceptance will be published separately so this implementation head stays fixed. Local tools: root Go1.24.0, compiler Go1.27.3, Node22.23.4, pinned React/ReactDOM19.3.1 and Chromium153. Six actual concurrent Luna6 XHigh workers filled the available six worker slots; native Rebalancer1.0.4 allocations and actual model deliveries are separate. Initial allocation and capacity evidence are in `compiled-lifecycle/coordination/`.\n\n[Reproduction](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/49cc2b96c8817a47319d5b7bd484184a22fa984b/compiled-lifecycle/README.md) · [bounded contract](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/49cc2b96c8817a47319d5b7bd484184a22fa984b/compiled-lifecycle/CONTRACT.md) · [fixed script](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/gondola/blob/49cc2b96c8817a47319d5b7bd484184a22fa984b/compiled-lifecycle/FIXTURE.md).\n\nScope: finite value-owned slots and a deterministic manual effect host, not arbitrary pointer-based Manager compilation or dynamic child graphs. AppIR v1's request/reply capability is coarse; another backend must explicitly implement the closed lifecycle effect profile, typed encoding and cancellation/callback protocol, then pass the same matrix. Other browser engines, IME, hydration, concurrent React, pixels and real network transport remain untested. No main merge or deployment.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-31T06:54:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-31T06:54:37Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d6fe98cd11cb8eb5ba673a449099b170e222b3fa","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"samuelpmahan:codex/gobi-compiled-lifecycle-20261031","ref":"codex/gobi-compiled-lifecycle-20261031","repo":{"id":1439172595,"node_id":"R_kgDOVcgH8w","name":"gondola","full_name":"samuelpmahan/gondola","owner":{"login":"samuelpmahan","id":32501459,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTAxNDU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32501459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"Go","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"op